Zero-initialize variables released by _cleanup_ attributes (OpenUI patch).

These variables are freed when the function returns, but were left uninitialized.
When an early step failed, e.g. es10c_get_eid in chip info, lpac freed stack garbage
and crashed before closing its logical channel. The same pattern remains in
upstream main (82ada9e) for chip info, notification process/replay/dump and the stdio
drivers.

